      "body": "## Overview\n\n`select_fp8_moe_backend()` rejected an explicit `moe_backend=\"cutlass\"` with a\nreason-free error. This makes that one branch report the actual reason, matching\nevery sibling backend in the same function. Fixes #62135.\n\n## Claims\n\n- The `cutlass` / batched-cutlass rejection now names the backend and the real\n  reason instead of the opaque `\"vLLM CUTLASS FP8 MoE backend is disabled for\n  this configuration.\"`.\n- Behavior is unchanged: the same configurations are still rejected; only the\n  error message improves.\n- Consistent with the sibling backends, which already route their rejections\n  through `_make_log_unsupported(backend, reason)` in the same call.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` (v0.14.0, the pinned pre-commit\n  version) pass on the changed file.\n- The module imports cleanly.\n- No existing test asserts the old message string, so no test needed updating.\n\n## Details\n\n`moe_backend=\"cutlass\"` is a legal value, but the vLLM-native CUTLASS FP8 MoE\nkernels are only enabled (`allow_vllm_cutlass=True`) for per-channel weight +\nper-token activation (PTPC) FP8 and compressed-tensors w8a8 FP8. For other FP8\nschemes (e.g. online `fp8_per_tensor`) the branch raised a message that did not\nsay why. The reason is now surfaced via the existing `_make_log_unsupported`\nhelper.\n\nScope is intentionally limited to the error-message inconsistency (problems 1\nand 2 in the issue). Moving this validation earlier to `create_engine_config()`\n(problem 3) is a larger change left for a follow-up.\n",
      "changedFiles": 1,
